  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Omicron Leonis",
    "description": "Multiple star in the constellation Leo",
    "summary": "Omicron Leonis is a binary star in the constellation of Leo, west of Regulus, some 130 light-years from the Sun, where it marks one of the lion's forepaws. The position of this system near the ecliptic means it is subject to lunar occultation.",
    "intro": "Omicron Leonis (ο Leonis, abbreviated Omicron Leo, ο Leo) is a binary star in the constellation of Leo, west of Regulus, some 130 light-years from the Sun, where it marks one of the lion's forepaws. The position of this system near the ecliptic means it is subject to lunar occultation.\nThe system consists of Omicron Leonis Aa (officially named Subra , the traditional name for the system) and Omicron Leonis Ab.",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Omicron_Leonis",
    "thumbnail": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Leo_constellation_map.svg/330px-Leo_constellation_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail",
